HHTP/HTTPS

Hyper text transfer protocol

Its a  protocol which is used to transfer the data from client(browser) nd server

User enters URL in browser
Browser sends HTTP request
Server processes it
Server sends HTTP response

HTTP-transfers the data in the form of plain text, and HTTPS -transfers data in encrypted fromat
HTTP+SSL=HTTPS
“HTTP is a protocol used for transferring data over the web, while HTTPS is its secure version that uses SSL/TLS encryption to protect data transmission.”

Uses SSL/TLS encryption (Transport Layer Security)
Data is encrypted before sending 🔐
Only intended receiver can decrypt
🔹 Features of HTTPS
Secure communication 🔒
Works on port 443
Uses SSL/TLS certificates
Protects against:
Data theft
Man-in-the-middle attacks
