DNS is sys that transfers domain name into IP adress so that browser can locate and connect to websites

1. User Request

You enter: www.google.com

2. DNS Resolver(recursive resolver)client_loop--here it will check in browser caching and os caching.then it will send to root user

3. Root Server

Resolver asks root DNS server

4. TLD Server

Then it goes to Top-Level Domain (TLD) server (.com, .org)

5. Authoritative Server

Finally reaches the authoritative DNS server

6. IP Address Returned

Server responds with IP → Browser connects to website

